-- A BOT THAT HELPS RUN A SERVER
--
-- The first bot, hello-bot, only listens for people talking. This one listens for everything:
-- slash commands, buttons, reactions, and people arriving and leaving. It is still a loop.
--
--     polite build examples/discord/club-bot.polite
--     cd examples/discord
--     npm install discord.js
--     node club-bot.mjs
--
-- It needs two things turned on where you got the token, under Privileged Gateway Intents:
-- Message Content Intent, and Server Members Intent for the arriving and leaving.
--
-- One thing worth knowing: the words that act on a person -- giving a role, quietening, renaming --
-- all act on whoever the last thing that happened was about. There is no way to reach across and
-- act on somebody else, which is deliberate: a bot that can only act on the person in front of it
-- is a much harder bot to turn into a weapon.
--
-- Written in PoliteLang by Creeperdiamonds Studios.


please define the welcome card:
    remember card is an empty lookup
    put "Welcome" for "title" in card
    put "Have a look at the rules, say hello, and make yourself at home." for "words" in card
    put "green" for "colour" in card
    put "Posted by a bot written in English" for "footer" in card
    give back card
thank you for defining


please define the menu:
    remember buttons is an empty list
    add "Rules" to buttons
    add "Roles" to buttons
    add "Who is here" to buttons
    give back buttons
thank you for defining


please show ""
please show "  A BOT THAT HELPS RUN A SERVER"
please show ""

-- Said before logging in, because it changes what Discord is asked for.
please watch people joining and leaving

please try to:
    log in to discord with the secret called "DISCORD_TOKEN"
    let my status be "keeping the place tidy"

    offer the command "hello" for "I will say hello back"

    remember takes is an empty list
    add "sides" to takes
    offer the command "roll" taking takes for "Roll a die with however many sides you like"

    show "  Commands offered. They appear straight away."
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  I could not start, because {what went wrong}"
    show ""
    stop everything
thank you for trying

please show "  Listening. Press control and C to stop."
please show ""

please keep going forever:
    -- Everything to do with one happening sits in here, so that one thing going wrong costs that
    -- one thing and not the whole evening.
    try to:
        listen for whatever happens next

        check if somebody joined:
            show "  {their name} arrived."
            try to:
                announce "Welcome, {their name}. There are {the people in the server} of us now." in the channel called "general"
            otherwise if it does not work out:
                show "    (no general channel to welcome them in)"
            thank you for trying

        otherwise if somebody left:
            show "  {their name} left."

        otherwise if it was a command:
            remember which is the command they used
            check if which is "hello":
                reply with "Hello, {their name}. Good to see you."
            otherwise if which is "roll":
                remember asked is what they gave for "sides"
                remember sides is the number in asked or 6
                check if sides is under 2:
                    change sides to 6
                thanks
                reply with "A die of {sides} sides came up {a random whole number from 1 to sides}."
            otherwise:
                reply quietly with "I do not know that one."
            thank you for checking

        otherwise if it was a button:
            remember pressed is the button they pressed
            check if pressed is "Rules":
                reply quietly with "Be kind. Stay on topic. That is the whole of it."
            otherwise if pressed is "Roles":
                reply quietly with "You have: {the join of the roles they have with ", "}."
            otherwise:
                reply quietly with "There are {the people in the server} of us, across {the number of items in the channels in the server} channels."
            thank you for checking

        otherwise if it was a reaction:
            show "  {their name} put {the emoji they used} on something."

        otherwise if it was a message:
            remember spoken is what they said
            remember said is the small letters of the trimmed version of spoken
            show "  {their name} in {the channel it came from}: {spoken}"

            check if they are a bot:
                show "    (a bot, so I left it alone)"
            otherwise if said is "!menu":
                present "What would you like to know?" with buttons the menu
            otherwise if said is "!welcome":
                post a card made of the welcome card
            otherwise if said is "!about":
                post a card titled "About me" saying "I am a Discord bot written entirely in English sentences, in a language called PoliteLang."
            otherwise if said is "!here":
                reply with "There are {the people in the server} of us in {the server it came from}."
            otherwise if said is "!me":
                reply with "You are {their name}, and Discord knows you as {their id}. Your roles: {the join of the roles they have with ", "}."
            otherwise if said is "!join":
                check if they have the role called "Member":
                    reply with "You already have that one."
                otherwise:
                    give them the role called "Member"
                    reply with "Done. You are a Member now."
                thank you for checking
            otherwise if said mentions "thank":
                react with "💛"
            otherwise if said is "!slowly":
                start typing
                wait for 2 seconds
                reply with "There. Worth waiting for, I hope."
            thank you for checking
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if it does not work out:
        show "    (that one did not work out: {what went wrong})"
    thank you for trying
thank you for repeating
